  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA n2000, single profile) achieves 48.5% accuracy while image-only (ResNet50) is very weak at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant signal. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether multiprofile aggregation improves RNA performance, which is a critical design axis that affects 6 of the 9 remaining RNA/multimodal configurations. This experiment (config_002) tests the single most important extension of our best result: changing from singleprofile to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation while keeping the same PCA n2000 encoder. It isolates the profile/aggregation effect with minimal variable change from config_001. If multiprofile helps, it justifies investing remaining budget in multiprofile variants; if not, we can focus on encoder quality (scvi, scgpt) instead. This is the highest-information experiment given 7 remaining slots."
}

